course: dictionary
lesson: 127
title: A word with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Advent is one of them. «Advent is the four weeks before Christmas, a time of waiting and getting ready.» Here it is the name of a church season, so it means the time before Christmas.
explain: Now read this: «The advent of the internet changed how we find things out.» There is no season in that sentence. The advent of something means its arrival or beginning, so the internet arrived and changed things.
explain: Ask which meaning fits. Put your meaning into the sentence: "the arrival of the internet" works, but "the four weeks before the internet" does not. The sentence will show you the right meaning.
explain: Clues can be objects too. Advent wreaths and calendars point to the church season, while the word "of" after advent, as in "the advent of", often points to the arrival meaning.
fact: Advent is a noun, and it has two meanings.
fact: «Advent» with a capital A means the church season of about four weeks before Christmas.
fact: In that season, Christians get ready to celebrate Jesus' birth and wait for his coming again.
fact: «The advent of something» means its arrival or beginning, as in «the advent of the internet».
fact: Useful phrases: advent calendar, advent wreath, the first Sunday of Advent.
exercise: «Advent is the four weeks before Christmas, a time of waiting and getting ready.» What does Advent mean here? | A kind of chocolate | *The church season before Christmas | The arrival of a new computer | A Christmas present
exercise: «The advent of the internet changed how we find things out.» What does advent of the internet mean? | The name of an inventor | A long wait for the internet | *Its arrival or beginning | Its end
exercise: Which phrase names a ring of candles that is lit one more each Sunday before Christmas? | Advent of the internet | Advent of trains | *Advent wreath | Christmas stocking
test: «Many churches use purple in Advent and Lent, white or gold at Christmas and Easter.» What is Advent in this sentence? | The arrival of a new season | A colour of paper | A Christmas song | *The church season before Christmas
test: «It begins with Advent, four weeks of getting ready, then Christmas for Jesus' birth.» What do the words four weeks tell you about Advent? | It is only for shops | It starts in summer | *It lasts about four weeks | It lasts one day
exam: The word advent has two meanings. In «the advent of the internet», which meaning fits and why? | The church season, because it comes before Christmas | *The formal meaning, arrival or beginning, because the internet arrived | Neither, because advent is a verb | The church season, because the internet has four weeks
